WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.190
Garstang, in the UK, 2000.

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.910
The Fair Trade Towns campaign begins.

3
00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:09.690
By 2017 there were over
2,000 Fair Trade Towns,

4
00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.970
in 29 countries.

5
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:18.450
Far away, in 2024, Fairtrade reported
1.87 million farmers and workers,

6
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:23.250
in 1,824 producer organisations.

7
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:25.490
Shoppers pay extra for the label.

8
00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:29.530
But do farmers, workers and
the environment actually gain?

9
00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.730
In this mission, you'll test
fair trade against its own aims:

10
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:37.310
fairer trade, safer work
and a cleaner environment.

11
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.690
Then you'll follow a binding
factory-safety agreement in Bangladesh,

12
00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.790
and check its record.

13
00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.880
Your mission: decide who actually gains
when shoppers choose ethical labels.
